Architecture plan for issues #79-#80

Project shape:
- Existing Next.js App Router app for myClawTeam Blog.
- Layout components live under components/layout/.
- App Router metadata and special files live under app/.
- Product contract and naming source is PRODUCT.md; visible brand remains "myClawTeam Blog".

Issue #79 — favicon:
- Add an App Router icon special file at app/icon.svg, derived from the myClawTeam brand mark/logo rather than a generic placeholder.
- Keep it self-contained in the repo so Next.js automatically emits the correct head metadata.
- Verify with the built app that the icon route/head link resolves.

Issue #80 — header/footer subtitle removal:
- Edit components/layout/site-header.tsx and components/layout/site-footer.tsx only.
- Remove the subtitle span text "Official updates and engineering notes" from logo/title blocks.
- Preserve the logo image, "myClawTeam Blog" visible brand text, existing links, styling structure, and homepage/metadata copy.

Dependencies and sequencing:
- The two issues are independent UI/static asset changes.
- #79 can be implemented without touching layout components.
- #80 should avoid metadata/homepage copy changes and only alter the specified header/footer subtitle nodes.

Key decisions:
- Use native Next.js App Router conventions instead of custom head management.
- Keep changes minimal and targeted to reduce risk to deployed blog/admin behavior.
- No new persistent storage, auth, or runtime service changes are required for either issue.
